{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And it went out.</b> Because they did not do it properly, for even though there is a commandment to bring fire from a layman, as it is written: ״ונתנו בני אהרן אש״ etc. — that is after it had descended from heaven once; but beforehand, one was not to bring from a layman, for it diminishes the honor of Heaven, for they would say: the offering was consumed by the fire of a layman. And according to this explanation, when they brought it, the fire descending from heaven met them. And there is a difficulty: for beforehand it is written: ״ותצא אש מלפני ה׳״. However, the Sages said in tractate Yoma that they died because they issued a ruling in the presence of Moses their master, for they expounded: ״ונתנו בני אהרן אש״ — even though fire descends from heaven, it is a commandment to bring from a layman." "<b>And they died before HaShem.</b> There is a dispute in Torat Kohanim. Rabbi Eliezer says: they died outside, in the place where the Levites are permitted to enter, as it is said: ״ויקרבו וישאום בכתנותם״ — if so, what is ״לפני ה׳״? The angel struck them and brought them outside. Rabbi Akiva says: they did not die except inside, as it is said: ״לפני ה׳״. And what is ״ויקרבו וישאום בכתנותם״? This teaches that they put a hook of iron into their mouths and dragged them and brought them outside. And there is a difficulty according to Rabbi Akiva: if so, the Tabernacle became impure, for it is called an ohel for the impurity of a corpse, and requires sprinkling on the third and seventh days, and we do not find that they ceased from their service at all. And likewise it is written explicitly: ״ומפתח אהל מועד לא תצאו״. This works well according to Rabbi Eliezer: the angel pushed them outside before the departure of the soul; but according to Rabbi Akiva it is difficult, and it requires investigation."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The phrase הורו הוראה בפני משה רבן appears to read 'their master' (רבן) on the basis of the standard Talmudic idiom (Yoma 53a: שהורו הלכה לפני רבן); translated as it stands.", 1 "Abbreviations resolved: רא\"א = Rabbi Eliezer (ha'Azari?); resolved as Rabbi Eliezer based on parallel in Torat Kohanim (Shemini 3). רע\"א = Rabbi Akiva, resolved on the same basis."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:04.639133557Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}